; The Rust target's cram test.  It is OPT-IN, and it has to be: it needs `spectec/specs/rust`,
; the PRIVATE `rust-spectec` submodule, and this repository is public.  A public clone deinits
; that submodule (README, "Installation"), after which the encoding and its test corpus are
; both absent and this test could only fail.
;
; `(alias rust)` alone is NOT enough -- measured in a scratch clone at Task 45 fix round 1: a
; `cram` stanza's `alias` field ADDS an alias, it does not move the test off `runtest`, so
; `dune test` still ran it and it still failed.  `enabled_if` is what takes it off, and
; `make test-rust`, which sets SPECTEC_RUST_TESTS=yes, is what turns it on.
(cram
 (alias rust)
 (enabled_if
  (= %{env:SPECTEC_RUST_TESTS=no} yes))
 (package spectec-target-rust)
 (deps
  %{bin:spectec}
  (package spectec-target-rust)
  ../../../../spectec-target-rust.install
  (source_tree ../../../specs/rust)
  (source_tree ../../../testdata/interp/rust)))
